{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":488224,"name":"aiaje com","username":"aiaje_com","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/919ad9/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-10T15:16:05.571Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488224-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488224-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488224-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488224-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn Windows, Grok Bot’s in-app updater downloads a new installer, then refuses to install it. Settings show: “다운로드한 업데이트를 확인할 수 없어 설치되지 않았어요” (The downloaded update could not be verified, so it was not installed.)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe app version stays on the old build. Seen on 0.36.0 stuck while 0.39.0 was current (2026-09-04), and again on 0.44.0 stuck while 0.47.0 was current (2026-09-10). %LOCALAPPDATA%\\sand-updater\\installer.exe remains the already-installed version.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe official Setup.exe from \u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/download/bot\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eCursor · Download Grok Bot\u003c/a\u003e has Authenticode status Valid and signer “Anysphere, Inc.” and installs correctly when run manually (Setup.exe /S).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is desktop app update, not Agent Computer image update/reset.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488224-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488224-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eInstall Grok Bot on Windows x64 (stable track, auto-update on).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWait until a newer stable is published on the official Grok Bot download page.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Settings → Updates → Check for Updates (or wait for auto-update).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDownload progress appears, then the unverified-install error. App FileVersion does not change.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488224-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488224-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter a successful download, the signed installer should be staged and applied on quit/restart, matching the version on the download page.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488224-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488224-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488224-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488224-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot 0.47.0 (Windows x64), currently installed after a manual official Setup.exe. Previously stuck at 0.36.0 then 0.44.0. Windows 11 10.0.26200.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488224-additional-information-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488224-additional-information-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e0.47.0 app.asar still contains the same probe: Get-AuthenticodeSignature via powershell.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command, then JSON.parse of stdout, requiring status === “Valid” and signer in [“Anysphere, Inc.”, “Anysphere”]. Failure kind: installer_signature_invalid (UI id VZlSAx). On failure the downloaded file is deleted.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnysphere installers use short-lived Microsoft ID Verified / Azure Trusted Signing certificates (~3 days) plus a timestamp. Get-AuthenticodeSignature from an interactive PowerShell session still returns Valid after NotAfter because of the timestamp. The in-app Electron execFile(“powershell.exe”, …, { windowsHide: true }) path can still fail (unreadable JSON, status not exactly Valid, unexpected SimpleName), which matches “download happened, install never started”.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSuggested fix: verify with WinVerifyTrust / timestamp-aware Authenticode without parsing PowerShell JSON; do not delete a just-downloaded installer on a probe parse error; don’t treat Agent Computer reset as the recovery path for this desktop-app failure.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOfficial installer that applied cleanly (0.47.0):\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ca href=\"https://downloads.cursor.com/grokbot/stable/win32-x64/0.47.0/Grok_Bot_0.47.0_Setup.exe\" class=\"onebox\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ehttps://downloads.cursor.com/grokbot/stable/win32-x64/0.47.0/Grok_Bot_0.47.0_Setup.exe\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488224-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488224-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-10T15:16:15.141Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":21,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":90.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":171265,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-windows-in-app-update-downloads-then-fails-authenticode-probe-installer-signature-invalid","display_username":"aiaje com","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://downloads.cursor.com/grokbot/stable/win32-x64/0.47.0/Grok_Bot_0.47.0_Setup.exe","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":0},{"url":"https://cursor.com/download/bot","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Cursor · Download Grok Bot","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":137178,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-windows-in-app-update-downloads-then-fails-authenticode-probe-installer-signature-invalid/171265/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":488748,"name":"Colin","username":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-11T09:06:40.088Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/aiaje_com\"\u003e@aiaje_com\u003c/a\u003e, thanks for the detailed report.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYour read is right: the in-app updater downloads the new installer, the verification step fails, and the file is removed, so the app stays on the old version.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom what we can see the same verification has gone through on your machine on other days, so the signing certificate itself is not the problem. It looks like something about the moment right after the download finishes (for example an antivirus still holding the file, or the check taking too long).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor now, installing the Setup.exe from \u003ca href=\"http://cursor.com/download/bot\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eCursor · Download Grok Bot\u003c/a\u003e is the right workaround. Your Agent Computer does not need a reset or update for this, it is only the desktop app.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you have a minute, one check would help us narrow it down. In a normal (non-admin) PowerShell window, run this against the installer you downloaded, replacing the path:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003eMeasure-Command { powershell.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command \"$ErrorActionPreference='Stop'; $sig = Get-AuthenticodeSignature -LiteralPath 'C:\\Path\\To\\Grok_Bot_0.47.0_Setup.exe'; [pscustomobject]@{ status = $sig.Status.ToString(); signer = $sig.SignerCertificate.GetNameInfo('SimpleName', $false) } | ConvertTo-Json -Compress\" | Out-Host }\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease reply with the JSON line it prints, the TotalSeconds value, and which antivirus or endpoint security product runs on that PC (Defender, V3, ALYac, etc.). If you can, also note whether the antivirus was scanning the next time an in-app update fails.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-11T09:06:40.088Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":0.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":171265,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-windows-in-app-update-downloads-then-fails-authenticode-probe-installer-signature-invalid","display_username":"Colin","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://cursor.com/download/bot","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Cursor · Download Grok Bot","clicks":1}],"read":true,"user_title":"Community Support Engineer","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_i